**What changed**

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `BrowsersSessionManager.vue` | New `sidebarCollapsed` data + `localStorage` persistence, `<aside>` animated `w-16 ↔ w-80`, mobile forced expanded |
| `BrowserSessionList.vue` | `collapsed` prop, icon rail mode, collapse/expand toggle button, `emits`, removed dead `mounted` method inside `methods` |

**Design decisions**

- **Initial-letter avatars** (`w-10 h-10`) instead of one generic glyph: identical icons are unscannable once there are more than three sessions; a letter monogram stays distinguishable in a 64px rail. Swap `{{ sessionInitial(session) }}` for `<i class="fa-solid fa-window-maximize"></i>` if you prefer a uniform glyph.
- **Native `title` instead of DaisyUI `tooltip tooltip-right`**: a rail longer than the viewport needs `overflow-y-auto`, which forces `overflow-x: auto` and clips `data-tip` pseudo-elements. Native titles never clip and still fire on keyboard focus.
- **Status dot** (`bg-success` / `bg-warning` / `bg-base-content/30`) keeps status readable without expanding, never relying on color alone (`title` + badge in expanded mode carry the same info).
- **`+` in the rail expands first**, then opens the create form — a 64px rail can't host inputs.
- Collapsed/expanded toggles preserve one accessible pattern: `aria-expanded` on the toggle, `aria-current="true"` on the selected session, `focus-visible:outline-2 outline-offset-2` (Tailwind 4 outline utilities, not the deprecated ring-offset) on the rail buttons.

**Accessibility checklist**

- [x] Toggle buttons 32px with `aria-label` + `aria-expanded`
- [x] Rail items 40px targets, 6px gap, `aria-current` marks selection
- [x] Session identity available to screen readers via `aria-label` (not only the letter)
- [x] Status conveyed by dot **and** the expanded badge label
- [x] Keyboard focus visible on every new control

**Anti-patterns avoided**: no `overflow: hidden` clipping on tooltips, no fixed `width` on the panel (`flex-1 min-w-0`), no color-only selection state, no >200ms animation on the width transition.

