I'll locate the component that renders the browser + chat ("SHARED ACTIVITY") so the splitter goes between the right elements.There's a `BrowserViewer.vue` I haven't seen yet — likely the browser + chat view. Let me read it plus the splitter API.Found it — the browser + chat view in your screenshots is **`src/components/browsers/BrowserViewer.vue`** (it renders the live iframe plus the "Shared activity" / AI-cost panel, currently stacked *below* the browser in a fixed `max-h-72` strip). I also read `VerticalSplitter.vue` to confirm its API (`show-handle`, `persist-key`, `show-right`, per-panel `minSize`/`defaultSize`; radix handles use pointer capture, so dragging works even over the iframe).

## Plan

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `BrowserViewer.vue` | Move the shared-activity/cost block from below the iframe into a **right-hand resizable panel** via `VerticalSplitter` (`persist-key="browsers.viewer"`, visible grip). Browser left (`minSize 40`, default 72%), chat/activity right (`minSize 18`, default 28%, collapsible). `compact` mode keeps the browser only (`:show-right="!compact"` — single iframe block, no duplication). Activity list scrolls, cost pinned at the bottom of the panel. |
| `BrowsersSessionManager.vue` | Remove the splitter between the sidebar and the session panel: the expanded sidebar goes back to a **fixed `w-80`** (collapsed stays `w-[68px]`), with the 200ms width transition restored. `VerticalSplitter` import dropped. |

