I need the current state of `BrowserViewer.vue` (the component holding the browser + shared activity) before changing it to a drawer.Found it — `src/components/browsers/BrowserViewer.vue` currently splits browser/activity with a `VerticalSplitter`. Per the new request, the **Shared activity + AI cost** panel becomes a **right-side drawer**, opened from an icon in a new **footer bar** (matching the `1 chat(s) · date` strip in your screenshot).

## Plan

| Concern | Decision |
|---|---|
| **Splitter removed** | The iframe takes the full `flex-1` area; `VerticalSplitter` import dropped. The old `splitter-layout:browsers.viewer` key becomes unused. |
| **Footer bar** | New slim footer (`border-t`, 32px row): left shows chat count + last-activity time, right shows total cost + the **activity toggle icon** with an event-count badge. |
| **Drawer** | DaisyUI `drawer drawer-end` (per project convention) scoped to the component (`h-full`, local overlay — not `fixed`), checkbox bound to `activityDrawerOpen`. Panel is `w-80 max-w-[85vw]`: activity list scrolls, AI-cost block pinned at the bottom, close button in the panel header. Escape closes. |
| **Behaviour** | Opening the drawer triggers a non-quiet `refreshSessionData()` so the list is fresh. `compact` mode keeps the footer (it's now the only entry point to activity) — the drawer overlays, so no width is stolen from the browser in any mode. |

