**What changed**

| Area | Before | Now |
|---|---|---|
| Footer `Chat` | Opened the big picker modal, always | `openLatestChat()` → dock the pane with the session's **latest** chat (`resolveLatestChatId` → `ensureChat({ chatId })`). Falls back to the backend default (create/reuse) when nothing is linked. |
| `Focus chat` | Reopened the picker | Keeps the current chat and focuses the composer (`ref="chatPane"` → first `textarea`). |
| Chat header | Static "Chat with this browser" + icon-only switch button | The chat **name is the switcher trigger** (chevron rotates), subtitle keeps the session name |
| Menu | — | `<role="menu">` under the header: chats of this session newest-first (name + last-activity time, `fa-check` on the active one), `New chat`, `All chats…` (the existing modal), spinner while the index loads |
| Esc / outside click | — | `mousedown` outside trigger+menu closes it; `Escape` closes it; both listeners removed on `beforeUnmount` |
| Session change | Reset chat pane | Also resets the menu, so a pending menu never points at the previous session |

**How "latest" is resolved**

1. `session.chat_ids` is the linked set (already used by the `3 chat(s)` counter).
2. Each id is resolved to metadata from the fetched chat index first, then the chats store cache.
3. Sorted by `lastMessageAt → updated_at → created_at` descending; ids without metadata keep the session order (backend appends, newest last).
4. `ensureChat` is called with that explicit `chatId`, so the backend reuses it instead of guessing.
5. The chat index is fetched **only once** and **only when** some linked chat is still unknown — a single linked chat short-circuits without any request.

**Why this shape**

- The picker stays available (`All chats…`), but it is no longer on the critical path: the first click must never block on a 7000-chat list.
- Selection lives in the pane header, right above the conversation it changes — no eye travel to a footer or a distant modal.
- The active chat is marked twice (`fa-check` + primary colour), never by colour alone.

**Not verified:** no shell in this session, so `npm run build` / lint was not run.

