**What changed**

| Area | Before | Now |
|---|---|---|
| "Latest" definition | `lastMessageAt → updated_at → created_at` from whatever metadata happened to be cached | `chatLastMessageAt()` — newest **message** stamp (`updated_at → timestamp → created_at`) across the chat's messages; falls back to `lastMessageAt → updated_at → created_at` only when no message is available |
| Ranking | Silent fallback to the last id in `chat_ids` | Sorted by that stamp desc; chats without a known stamp keep session order (backend appends, newest last) |
| No chat found | `ensureChat({ chatId: null })` → backend created/reused a chat silently | Pane stays closed and the **chat selector dialog opens**; the backend is only called once a chat id (or "new chat") is chosen |
| Chat header | Only the title was a trigger (chevron), no dedicated affordance | Added an explicit `fa-solid fa-arrow-right-arrow-left` circle button ("Switch chat") next to the badge — spinner while loading, `btn-active` while the menu is open, `aria-haspopup`/`aria-expanded` |
| Menu opening | Listed chats that had no metadata yet (`Chat 3f2a…`) | `toggleChatMenu()` fetches the chat index first when any linked chat is unknown, so names and dates are real |
| Menu content | "New chat" then "All chats…" | "All chats…" first (that is where a linked chat may be missing from the list), then "New chat"; count in the header |
| Picker list | Order by `updated_at` | Order by last updated message, same rule as the switcher; each row shows that date |
| Pane visibility | Shown before the chat resolved | `showChat` set only after a chat is resolved, so a failed resolution never leaves an empty pane |

Notes
- Same chat selected → just refocuses the composer instead of re-requesting.
- Outside-click handler now also ignores the new switch button, so clicking it toggles instead of closing-then-reopening.
- `aria-expanded`/`aria-haspopup` on both triggers, active chat marked by `fa-check` **and** primary colour.

